A||||3||LottaBallsCamaro||Can the blower off a FWD 3.8 work on a 3.8 from a camaro?||||1||
Z||000000||LottaBallsCamaro||12-02-2001||03:25 PM||||Also, does it sit higher then a stock intake and will it fit under a non-bulged hood? Thanks!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||David DeVoe||12-02-2001||04:54 PM||||I build the 3800 here in Flint, MI. I don't know about the hood clearance question but I can tell you that there are many different parts in the supercharger engine. The heads are different, the pistons are different (lower compression) the harmonic balancer is different so is the lower intake manifold. It's not as easy as just bolting on a blower I'm afraid. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||PBJ||12-02-2001||04:59 PM||||The bottem end of a vin 1 is alot different then vin k, just as mentioned above.  Any thing is possible!  But I think  starting with a vin 1 with a s/c would be the best way to go.  I am sure you could find a market for the old engine.<p>[This message has been edited by PBJ (edited 12-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Pontiaddict||12-02-2001||08:54 PM||||The main problem is that the throttle body on the 3800sc is on the transaxle side of the motor. If you put it on a Camaro the throttle body would be at the back of the engine. If you can fit the s/c to the car, you would then have to make some ductwork to place the t/b at the right end of the motor.<BR>||||reg||1
